{"author":{"id":"a51b5961cc6de343a64125d8eb6a0f965aa434020b9c46ed932a1bbf143eb532"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1791565403,"nonce":"8OHEtJmgX/L1qhFzhSaj9dNj8dY=","message":"Design for compile-time CSS in TypeScript (user, 2026-10-09: TS preprocessing for compile-time CSS to TS structs). Prototyped against blinc_abi's blinc-css and TypeScript 6.0.3.\n\n**A stylesheet import**\n- `import sheet, { classes, vars, keyframes } from './card.css'`. A build-time transform, an unplugin like unplugin-typegpu so it serves Vite, Rollup, esbuild, webpack and Bun alike, compiles the sheet with blinc_abi's CSS engine through the addon, which Node can load at build time. It fails the build with each error at its file, line and column (this.error with loc), as a compile error.\n- The module's default export is the compiled sheet (blinc_abi BCSS bytes, inlined as base64 for a Node target): the native engine loads it with no parsing and no string per rule crossing N-API (see ede8ea0). The named exports are frozen objects of the names the sheet defines: classes, custom properties and keyframes.\n- Types: the transform also writes card.d.css.ts beside the sheet. TypeScript reads it for './card.css' with allowArbitraryExtensions (TS 5.0+), so names are literal types, `classes.titel` is a compile error (TS2551, 'Did you mean title?'), and editors complete class names. This was checked with tsc on a prototype.\n- Structs for code that reads rules: an optional named export, `rules`, the sheet as a readonly typed literal (selectors, declarations, media), for a framework or a devtool that inspects styles; tree-shaken when not imported, so the bytes stay the only cost.\n\n**Style objects written in TypeScript**\n- `const s = css({ card: { padding: '8px', color: 'red' } })`, typed against a property map generated from blinc_abi's property table (names and value types), so a wrong property or value is a type error. The same transform compiles the call at build time into the same bytes and class atoms and replaces it with the reference (static extraction, as StyleX and vanilla-extract do). What cannot be known at build time stays a run-time call.\n\n**Without a bundler**\n- `blinc-css` (or an npm bin wrapping the addon) in watch mode writes card.css.js and card.d.css.ts, for tsc-only builds.\n\n**Order:** after the N-API binding of the CSS engine. First the .css import with bytes, names and the .d.css.ts, then the rules export, then css({...}) extraction.","files":null}]}